Chapter: VirtioBlkMmioUndeclared
  cites Foreword chapter VirtioBlk

 The row on VirtioBlk's `-auto` entry points is only worth carrying if it
 refuses somebody. This calls one from an opening that declares Console and
 nothing else: the program drives a block device and says it does not, so
 the effect row is undeclared and the unit must not compile.

 Without this arm the row is an assertion with no runner, which is the shape
 the 1.34 entry itself warned about.

Section: Definitions

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    n <- (vb-capacity-auto 167772160 512 8)
    print-line-uni ("sectors: " & show n)
  end
